## 1. What is JDBC?

JDBC (Java Database Connectivity) is Java's standard API for talking to relational databases. It provides a uniform interface — the same Java code works with MySQL, PostgreSQL, Oracle, SQLite, etc. You just swap the driver.

```
Your Java Code
      │
      ▼
┌─────────────────┐
│   JDBC API      │   (java.sql.* — interfaces)
│   (standard)    │
└────────┬────────┘
         │
         ▼
┌─────────────────┐
│   JDBC Driver   │   (vendor-specific implementation)
│   (e.g., MySQL) │
└────────┬────────┘
         │
         ▼
┌─────────────────┐
│   Database      │   (MySQL, PostgreSQL, Oracle, etc.)
└─────────────────┘
```

**C# equivalent:** `ADO.NET` (`System.Data`) — same concept. JDBC = ADO.NET, JDBC Driver = Data Provider (SqlClient, Npgsql).

