## 5. Statement — Executing Queries

`Statement` executes static SQL — the SQL string is sent directly to the database.

```java
try (Connection conn = DriverManager.getConnection(url, user, password);
     Statement stmt = conn.createStatement()) {

    // SELECT — returns a ResultSet
    ResultSet rs = stmt.executeQuery("SELECT id, name, salary FROM employees");
    while (rs.next()) {
        int id = rs.getInt("id");
        String name = rs.getString("name");
        double salary = rs.getDouble("salary");
        System.out.println(id + " | " + name + " | " + salary);
    }

    // INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE — returns affected row count
    int rowsAffected = stmt.executeUpdate(
        "INSERT INTO employees (name, salary) VALUES ('Alice', 75000)"
    );
    System.out.println(rowsAffected + " row(s) inserted");

    // DDL (CREATE TABLE, ALTER, DROP)
    stmt.execute("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS logs (id INT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY, msg TEXT)");

} catch (SQLException e) {
    e.printStackTrace();
}
```

### Three Execute Methods

| Method | Use For | Returns |
|--------|---------|---------|
| `executeQuery(sql)` | SELECT | `ResultSet` |
| `executeUpdate(sql)` | INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, DDL | `int` (row count) |
| `execute(sql)` | Any SQL (when you don't know the type) | `boolean` (true if ResultSet) |

**⚠️ NEVER use `Statement` with user input — vulnerable to SQL injection!**

```java
// ❌ SQL INJECTION — attacker sends: name = "'; DROP TABLE employees; --"
String name = userInput;
stmt.executeQuery("SELECT * FROM employees WHERE name = '" + name + "'");
// Becomes: SELECT * FROM employees WHERE name = ''; DROP TABLE employees; --'

// ✓ Use PreparedStatement instead (next section)
```

