## 7. ResultSet — Reading Results

`ResultSet` is a cursor that iterates over rows returned by a SELECT query:

```java
ResultSet rs = pstmt.executeQuery();

// Iterate rows
while (rs.next()) {   // moves cursor to next row, returns false at end
    // Read by column name (preferred — readable)
    int id = rs.getInt("id");
    String name = rs.getString("name");
    double salary = rs.getDouble("salary");
    boolean active = rs.getBoolean("active");
    Date hireDate = rs.getDate("hire_date");

    // Read by column index (1-based — faster but fragile)
    int id2 = rs.getInt(1);
    String name2 = rs.getString(2);
}
```

### Handling NULLs

```java
double salary = rs.getDouble("salary");
if (rs.wasNull()) {
    // The last value read was SQL NULL
    System.out.println("Salary is null");
}

// Or use getObject() which returns null for SQL NULL
Integer age = (Integer) rs.getObject("age");   // null if SQL NULL
```

### ResultSet Getter Methods

| SQL Type | Java Method | Java Type |
|----------|-------------|-----------|
| INT | `getInt()` | `int` |
| BIGINT | `getLong()` | `long` |
| FLOAT/DOUBLE | `getDouble()` | `double` |
| DECIMAL | `getBigDecimal()` | `BigDecimal` |
| VARCHAR/TEXT | `getString()` | `String` |
| BOOLEAN | `getBoolean()` | `boolean` |
| DATE | `getDate()` | `java.sql.Date` |
| TIMESTAMP | `getTimestamp()` | `java.sql.Timestamp` |
| BLOB | `getBytes()` / `getBlob()` | `byte[]` / `Blob` |

