## 11. CallableStatement — Stored Procedures

Call database stored procedures and functions:

```sql
-- MySQL stored procedure
DELIMITER //
CREATE PROCEDURE get_employees_by_dept(IN dept_name VARCHAR(50))
BEGIN
    SELECT * FROM employees WHERE department = dept_name;
END //
DELIMITER ;
```

```java
String sql = "{CALL get_employees_by_dept(?)}";

try (Connection conn = getConnection();
     CallableStatement cs = conn.prepareCall(sql)) {

    cs.setString(1, "Engineering");
    ResultSet rs = cs.executeQuery();

    while (rs.next()) {
        System.out.println(rs.getString("name"));
    }
}
```

### With OUT Parameters

```sql
CREATE PROCEDURE count_employees(IN dept VARCHAR(50), OUT total INT)
BEGIN
    SELECT COUNT(*) INTO total FROM employees WHERE department = dept;
END;
```

```java
String sql = "{CALL count_employees(?, ?)}";
try (CallableStatement cs = conn.prepareCall(sql)) {
    cs.setString(1, "Engineering");           // IN parameter
    cs.registerOutParameter(2, Types.INTEGER); // OUT parameter
    cs.execute();

    int count = cs.getInt(2);   // read OUT parameter
    System.out.println("Count: " + count);
}
```

